# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch I."""
DESC_I = {
    "PT": {
        47: "Julie's younger sister.\nA spirited girl, she fought alongside the men as a member of the Cosmo Factory. After being wounded, she happened upon Teral, who was fleeing Gagaan's pursuers, and tended to his injuries. Learning that even among the Elder - whom she had only ever hated - there were those capable of kindness, she reconsidered her one-sided view of them.\nAfterward, she saved Teral's life twice over: once from the Factory members who insisted he should be executed, and once from the gunfire of the pursuing Elder soldiers.",
        48: "Toshiya's father.\nAs chairman of the Cosmo Factory, he served as the leader of Io's inhabitants. After escaping the Elder's attack, he has led the surviving residents in a life on the run.\nHe is a man who makes calm decisions without being swept up by emotion or circumstance. When the Factory members, driven by anger, demanded that Teral - then being pursued by Gagaan - be executed, Taichiro instead decided he should be handed over as a prisoner to Dr. Kazami, and won the others over to his view.",
        49: "A young man belonging to the Free Space Force. Nineteen years old.\nIn the year 2062, before the world descended into spacetime chaos, he and Olson were partners both on and off duty.\nDispatched on a mission to destroy an orbital elevator occupied by hostile forces, Kei fought to protect the spacetime vibration bomb at the heart of the operation, but the enemy's fierce assault forced a retreat. Along the retreat route, he discovered an unadjusted spacetime vibration bomb, and in a bid to strike back at the enemy, he activated it.\nCaught up in the spacetime chaos this unleashed, the world plunged into the Chaos Century, dragging parallel universes into the upheaval along with it. Kei became an Anomaly and was cast twenty years into the future.",
        50: "A young man of nineteen who came to be known as the Anomaly in a world sealed within the Realm of Conflict.\nHe seems at first glance a typical hot-blooded, straightforward hero type, but underneath he is easygoing to a fault and an incorrigible womanizer. Even in the world before the spacetime chaos, he carried on relationships with countless women, and with one girlfriend in particular, Tina, he kept up secret trysts between military duties.\nAfter being transported to the world twenty years later, he was rescued by the Emaan caravan of the Factory led by Shaya, who told him he was the Anomaly. Learning that he himself was the cause of the world's turmoil, and that his existence was needed to repair it, he resolved to travel with the Factory.\nWhile mainly courting Mimsy, he also made passes at other women he spotted along the way, repeatedly stirring up trouble.\nHe possesses a natural talent for piloting: the inertial control system, an unfamiliar technology to him, he mastered after only a brief explanation and a little practice. Piloting the Molaba and the Orguss, he repeatedly drove back the Chiram army as it pursued Gloma in an attempt to seize the Anomaly.",
        51: "An Emaan woman who serves as chief of the Factory.\nStudious and thoughtful by nature, but also worldly-naive and far too much on her own wavelength.\nEmaan women have a fertile period, after which they lose their reproductive function. However, their bodies undergo almost no further change afterward, so even though she is already nearing thirty, Shaya still retains a youthful appearance. Emaan people also lose their sense of sexual modesty once their fertile period ends, so they think nothing of exposing themselves. Even a seasoned playboy like Kei was left stunned when she calmly walked into the bath while he was using it.\nThough born into the prestigious Tobu family, she left politics to her twin sister and continued her carefree life with the caravan - until she encountered Kei. Learning that he was the Anomaly needed to repair the spacetime chaos, she decided to protect him. This choice, however, put her at odds not only with Chiram but with her own sister Manisha, a fact that weighs heavily on her.",
        52: "An Emaan girl of seventeen, born in the Chaos Century.\nShe comes from the Raas family, a prominent house among the Emaan, and is its heir.\nShe met Kei while gaining experience with the caravan as a member of the Factory. She already had a fiance in the Factory, Sley, but found herself drawn to the forward Kei, and her heart wavered.\nLike other Emaan, Mimsy apparently has a twin sister as well, but she is said to lack an active personality and did not join the caravan.",
        53: "A humanoid built on Mu. Her appearance is indistinguishable from a human girl's.\nSwept up in a spacetime transfer and carried to Atlantis, she was put up for sale there. Kei bought her, and she became a member of Gloma.\nDesigned to become friends with humans, she possesses emotional circuits equivalent to a human's. As a result, she gradually came to fall in love with Kei, who was also her benefactor.\nHaving been built for nursing and repair work, she handled a wide range of tasks, from everyday chores to mechanical maintenance.",
        54: "Lieea's twin older sister.\nA spirited girl who bravely confronts the enemy in her Molaba whenever battle breaks out.\nBecause Emaan have a limited reproductive period, they are normally born as twins. However, as far as anyone has observed, these two sisters are practically the only twin pair who act together, which makes them a rare and valuable pair in more ways than one.",
        55: "Maaie's twin younger sister.\nShe is every bit as much of a tomboy as her sister. She sometimes bristles with rivalry at Maaie's older-sister airs, but the two generally get along well.\nShe has the nerve to climb into her own Molaba and fight aerial battles, but since she is not a soldier, she hesitates to harm a person directly.",
        56: "A member of a parallel-universe branch of humanity with a dinosaur-like appearance.\nHe is searching for a lover from whom he was separated during a spacetime transfer.\nWith a burner built into his mouth, he repeatedly breathed fire to drive off attacking Mozuku raiders, and during trading runs he instead put that same fire-breathing to use drawing in customers. He also proved useful in other ways, such as when he used his keen sense of smell to locate a vineyard after Gloma ran out of trade goods. He is also the one who named the Orguss.\nHe remembers the sensation of the spacetime transfer he once experienced, and can sense its warning signs through his tail's reactions, which has more than once let Gloma avoid disaster.",
        57: "An engineer with the Factory.\nWhen Kei's Bronco II was wrecked, Reeg used his own technical skill to repair and modify it, building the Orguss.",
        58: "An Emaan man and member of the Factory.\nPhysically weak and slight of build, he gives an androgynous impression. He is Mimsy's fiance, and hopes to be joined with her before her fertile second period of development - during which she is able to bear children - comes to an end, but he has struggled since she will not accept him.\nWhen Kei suddenly appeared and began pursuing Mimsy, Sley turned his hostility on him, at one point even pressing Shaya to drive Kei out.\nHis feelings for Mimsy are genuine: when she was nearly carried off by a Mozuku warrior, he picked an obviously unwinnable fight to protect her.",
        59: "An old man who travels with the Factory.\nA born merchant, he thinks nothing of shady dealings, such as passing off scraps of battle mecha as precious gems to sell to unsuspecting Atlantans.\nHe and Kei seemed to get along well, sharing drinks together and playing a game similar to Othello.",
        60: "An Emaan woman and member of the Factory.\nHer husband was killed by Chiram soldiers, and she now raises her surviving twin babies, Vee and Rom, as her sole reason for living.\nShe helps out with a variety of tasks aboard Gloma, from mechanical maintenance to manning the machine guns.",
        61: "A robot warrior built on Mu two hundred years ago, designed for close-quarters combat and mid- to short-range ground warfare. His rank is, fittingly, Captain.\nHe was a combat commander attached to the 11th Combat Squadron of the 22nd Battalion, Eslina Area Army, but was caught in a spacetime transfer during battle and thrown into the European region, where he shut down.\nWhen Gloma fled into Europe to escape Chiram, Kei and Mome, scavenging for salvageable junk, found and repaired him, and he became a member of Gloma.\nHis excessive pride often got in the way of swift action, and he was reluctant to use Emaan weapons, which more than once left him out of step with those around him. But once he is truly committed, his combat ability is a sight to behold.",
        62: "Kei's girlfriend in the world before the spacetime chaos.\nHer father never approved of her relationship with Kei, so the two carried on secret trysts, during which she conceived Kei's child, Athena.\nThe world soon plunged into the Chaos Century. She gave birth while Kei was missing, and raised their daughter alone, without a father present, ever after.\nIn the eighteenth year of the Chaos Century, she was caught in a Mu attack and died without ever being reunited with Kei.",
        63: "The daughter of Kei and Tina, born on February 20 of the second year of the Chaos Century. Eighteen years old.\nShe enlisted as a child soldier in the Chiram army from the age of eleven and worked as a soldier from then on. She met Olson when he was placed under the protection of her grandfather Michael, and came to see in him her image of an ideal father.\nWhen her mother and grandfather were later killed in a Mu attack, she resolved to fight not for revenge, but so that no one else would have to suffer the same grief she had. She volunteered for a transfer to the front line, where Olson drilled her in combat technique. The result was a first-rate woman warrior, combining a woman's delicacy with the bloodline of a gifted pilot.\nToward the father she has never even seen, she harbors both the loneliness of his absence and resentment for the hardship he caused her mother and grandfather.",
        64: "A young man belonging to the Free Space Force. Twenty years old.\nIn the year 2062, before the world descended into spacetime chaos, he fought alongside his best friend Kei as a team.\nSerious and strongly responsible almost to the point of rigidity, he seems every inch the soldier, but only when together with Kei did he ever let his youthful true self show.\nCaught in the explosion of the spacetime vibration bomb that Kei set off, he became a second Anomaly and was cast fifteen years into the future.",
        65: "A young man who came to be known as the other Anomaly in a world sealed within the Realm of Conflict.\nHe was born the same year as Kei, but because he appeared in the chaotic spacetime five years earlier, his lived age is also five years greater, making him twenty-five.\nWhen he appeared in the Chaos Century, he came under the protection of Chiram army General Michael Henderson. Through that connection he met the general's beloved daughter Tina, and likewise his granddaughter Athena. After Tina and Michael were killed in a Mu attack, he became Athena's guardian and instructor, supporting her both publicly and privately without ever revealing the feelings he kept hidden.\nIn recognition of his importance as an Anomaly and his achievements from before the spacetime chaos, he was granted the extraordinary rank of Special Major General in the Chiram army.",
        66: "Commander of the Chiram army's Tran Garrison. His rank is Captain.\nAs a battle-hardened veteran, he is the type to fixate on honors and military achievements.\nHe initially acted to capture Kei, the Anomaly, but his objective later shifted to assassination following a change in orders. He continued to relentlessly pursue Kei, including the traitor Olson, but failed time and again.\nWhen he proved unable to complete his mission and was about to be relieved of command, he and his subordinates confronted his superior officer Wesley and pleaded for the mission to continue. Given one last chance, he set out for the front line himself.",
        67: "Deputy commander of the Chiram army's Tran Garrison.\nCalm and composed, he ably assists Commander Roberto, whom he holds in high esteem. He always takes the lead in the operations to capture the Anomaly, but fails time and again.\nWhen he and Roberto were about to be pulled from the mission, he pressed their superior officer Wesley - in something close to a threat - to let them continue, and won one last chance.",
        68: "Shaya's twin younger sister.\nSince her older sister, who should rightfully be head of the family, is off on a carefree trading journey, Manisha has become the de facto head of the Tobu family in her place.\nShe clashed with the Raas family, Mimsy's household, over how to handle Kei, and asked him to help repair the spacetime chaos with the Emaan at its center. Her heavy-handed approach, however, provoked resistance, and her proposal was refused. She then showed herself willing to go so far as to brainwash Kei, which put her at odds with her own sister as well.",
        69: "President of Chiram and supreme commander of its military. His full name is Jeffrey White.\nHe issued the order to capture the Anomaly in order to repair the chaotic spacetime world and erase Mu, Chiram's greatest enemy. He later pushed forward 'Plan D,' a scheme to repair the world by artificially triggering another spacetime vibration through mechanical means.\nEven as he offered peace, he secretly plotted to brainwash Kei and Olson, hiding a ruthlessness that will order any means necessary to achieve his ends. Yet everything he does is for the greater cause of Chiram's survival, and he himself is a selfless man.",
        70: "Commander of a Chiram army frontline base. His rank is Lieutenant General.\nHe moved to relieve Roberto's unit from its mission to assassinate the Anomaly after their repeated failures, but ultimately granted them one last chance after facing what amounted to a threatening direct appeal.",
        71: "A young scientist living on Planet S-1. Twenty years old.\nAlongside his father, Dr. Reigan, and his colleagues, he worked on developing a radiation filtration and circulation system to save Planet S-1 from radioactive contamination. However, Gattler's faction framed him for the emperor's assassination and executed his father and colleagues in a coup. In the process, Marin killed Aphrodia's younger brother Milan, and he and Aphrodia became bitter enemies, each hating the other as the one who took someone dear to them.\nHe boarded the Pulsarvern, a subspace-capable spacecraft his father had developed, and pursued Gattler, but was caught up in the warp of a subspace fortress and crash-landed on the surface of the moon. He was taken prisoner by Blue Fixer while lying unconscious. Because he holds an intense longing for the nature already lost on Planet S-1, when he first saw Earth's oceans and skies, their beauty moved him to tears.\nHe was originally an approachable, cheerful, and likeable young man, but the string of misfortunes he suffered, combined with the frustration of not being trusted by those around him, sometimes led him to lash out at Blue Fixer members in fits of rage.\nHe later volunteered to join Blue Fixer in order to defeat his archenemy Gattler, and with the birth of Baldios, he gradually began to open his heart to his fellow Blue Fixer members.",
        72: "A special member of Blue Fixer's Special Task Force, and the pilot of the New Pulsarvern and Baldios.\nBecause he is an alien, he was at first suspected of being a spy and met with strong resistance within the base. But through his own actions he gradually won the crew's trust, and his outstanding piloting skill and knowledge of subspace mechanics eventually earned him the position of Baldios's main pilot.\nHe holds firmly to the belief that whatever he judges to be right must be carried out, and he will rush to the aid of comrades or loved ones in danger even at the cost of violating orders. But that conviction is a double-edged sword that can also become a liability - as shown when he was prepared to kill Marie, the news director of World Broadcasting, to protect Baldios's secret when she tried to uncover the truth about the Blue Fixer base.\nAt heart, though, he is a pure-hearted young man who secretly loves Earth's beauty even more than Earth's own people do. Precisely because of this, his determination to defeat Gattler is fierce, and his anger toward Aldebaron, which seeks to engulf Earth in war, burns like a raging fire within him.\nHe seems to be hopeless when it comes to romance: when Jamie invited him to a concert, he showed up at the meeting place with Raita and Oliver in tow, an oblivious response that hurt her feelings.\nThough he and Aphrodia remain enemies, their exchanges through battle seem to have struck a chord somewhere in his heart.",
        73: "A corporal in Blue Fixer's Special Task Force and pilot of the Baldy Prize. Twenty-two years old.\nBorn in the slums, he was placed in a care facility together with his younger sister Emily after their parents separated when he was ten. He volunteered for the Blue Fixer Youth Corps at twelve, and it was there that he met Raita, who has been his best friend ever since.\nCheerful and quick to show his feelings, he has the temperament of a delinquent who won't back down from anything he can't stand. When he was captured by Aldebaron and nearly turned into a spy with a mind control device, he cut himself with a knife rather than lose himself, holding on to his sanity through sheer resistance. Having survived a poor and rough childhood, he also exploded with anger at the World Federation's use of force to put down rioters when Aldebaron's destruction of Earth's crops caused a food shortage, and personally led an assault on the Federation's warehouses.\nYet he is by no means a crude man: he keeps a Bible close at hand as his constant companion, and he has quietly continued to carry a torch for Jamie, hinting at an innocent side beneath the surface.",
        74: "A sergeant in Blue Fixer's Special Task Force and pilot of the Caterranger. Twenty-one years old. He also works as a part-time night-school instructor at the military academy.\nHe hails from Little Japan, a facility built at point M-29 on the moon, and is the sole survivor of a spaceship accident that wiped out all its other residents. He was raised afterward in a care facility, enlisted in the Blue Fixer Youth Corps at eleven, and went on through the military academy before joining the Blue Fixer forces.\nA stubborn man of simple, sturdy virtue and deep feeling. He refuses to let others take on dangerous missions in his place, and is himself the brave sort who volunteers first.\nWhen Marin first joined the unit, Raita did not trust him at all, and their exchanges often escalated from verbal spats into outright fistfights. But as they weathered life-and-death situations together, Raita came to feel Marin's resolve firsthand and grew to trust him completely.",
        75: "A staff member of the Applied Physics Laboratory within Blue Fixer's Science Development Bureau. Eighteen years old.\nShe lived alone with her mother from a young age, but after her mother's death she was raised by a Greek family of Japanese descent. Following her adoptive parents' deaths she entered a care facility, and at fifteen volunteered for the World Federation Forces.\nShe wears her emotions plainly and cannot bring herself to abandon someone in trouble. She normally works under Quinstein, but she is an active young woman who, depending on the mission, willingly joins Marin and the others in actual combat.\nHer father's identity was unknown, but during a mission to the Kingdom of Bard, it came to light that the King of Bard himself was her father.\nThat she was convinced early on that Marin could be trusted shows just how perceptive she truly is. Perhaps it was inevitable that, in touching and gently unraveling his pure but lonely heart with her compassion, she should gradually find herself drawn to him.",
        76: "Commander-in-chief of Blue Fixer, an independent organization under the World Federation. Forty years old. He formerly served as director of the World Federation's Far East Branch.\nHe initially treated Marin as a suspected spy, but was moved by Marin's love for Earth and welcomed him into Blue Fixer as a fellow fighter.\nOwing to his position, he tends to be excessively hard on himself - even when word came of danger to the wife and child he had left behind in Japan, he suppressed his urge to go help them and tried to ignore it. He is also a good leader with the fairness to speak his mind, undeterred by rank or position, whenever someone is clearly in the wrong.\nHe shows real concern for his subordinates as well, such as throwing birthday parties to reward the hard-worked Blue Fixer members. To his troops, he is equal to a father as much as a commanding officer. Away from work, though, he is an ordinary middle-aged man whose hobbies are watching classic films and jogging every morning.",
        77: "A scientist with Blue Fixer and director of its Science Development Bureau. Thirty-two years old.\nAs the leader supporting Blue Fixer on the technical side, she developed a range of mecha, chief among them the Baldy Prize and Caterranger. Most notable is her analysis and modification of the Pulsarvern - the pinnacle of Planet S-1's subspace engineering - to build Baldios, a feat of insight and technical skill that speaks to her extraordinary ability and expertise as a scientist.\nShe once held a position in a research lab at Sunbridge University, but resigned after the World Federation ordered a halt to joint research she was conducting with her mentor and lover, Nerudo, on the grounds that it risked being converted into a weapon. She then volunteered for the World Federation Forces and has devoted herself to Earth's defense ever since.\nA strong-willed, quiet woman, she suppresses her emotions and throws herself into her duty. Harsh with herself and others alike, she shot Nerudo without hesitation when he misused the 'Vacuum Box,' one of her own past research achievements, as a weapon. Yet her granting the final wish of her student David, who was heading toward certain death, shows that she is without doubt a deeply compassionate person underneath.\nShe also has a sharp eye for talent: among the crew members who suspected Marin of being an alien spy, she was the first to recognize his knowledge of subspace mechanics and his high piloting skill, and requested his cooperation as a pilot for Baldios.",
        78: "A pilot candidate for Blue Fixer's Special Task Force.\nHe came to the Blue Fixer base as second pilot of the New Pulsarvern. His nihilistic air and provocative manner make him easy to misjudge, but underneath he is a man with a burning soul who will readily throw his life away for a cause he believes in.\nHe is Quinstein's former student and has carried romantic feelings for her since his school days, though he knows they can never be returned, which torments him.\nWhen Aldebaron moved the moon Ganymede to block out the sun, David volunteered in Marin's place to pilot the suicide weapon Fixer 1 to destroy it. His motive was not to protect Earth, but to protect Quinstein alone.\nThanks to his looks and the manner of his death, he was a highly popular character when the show originally aired. In the later theatrical film, he is given noticeably favorable treatment, even briefly piloting Baldios.",
        79: "Supreme commander-in-chief of Aldebaron. Twenty-five years old.\nShe lost her parents in a traffic accident at thirteen and was raised, together with her younger brother Milan, by Gattler. She became captain of Gattler's personal guard at twenty-three and rose to her current position after the coup succeeded. She holds strong trust and loyalty toward Gattler, and even when a classmate from military academy told her that it was Gattler who had had her parents assassinated, her devotion never wavered.\nHer skill as a commander is exceptional; in Gattler's stead, she personally handles everything from devising strategy to directing operations on the ground. She also has a ruthless side, having established a merciless code under which failure is paid for with death, and having lured and murdered those who stood in the way of herself or Gattler. Even so, many resent that she holds the post of commander-in-chief simply by virtue of being the Fuhrer's trusted right hand.\nWhen Marin killed her beloved brother Milan during the raid on the Reigan Institute, she came to hate him intensely. Because of this, she sometimes loses her usual composure and is swept away by raw emotion whenever she faces him.",
        80: "Fuhrer of the Aldebaron military. He also holds the concurrent posts of Chairman of the Unification Council and Chairman of the Joint Chiefs, making him the de facto dictator ruling the people of Planet S-1. Thirty-eight years old.\nNot only does he possess exceptional ability as a soldier, but his charisma and drive let him win the hearts of the populace in an instant, marking him as a leader of considerable stature.\nOn Planet S-1, he served as captain of Emperor Torinomias III's personal guard and repeatedly petitioned for an escape from the radiation-contaminated planet. But growing impatient with the emperor, who deferred to the scientists working toward restoring the environment, he used the Aldebaron military to carry out the emperor's assassination. He then pinned the blame on Marin and had the scientists, who stood in his way, executed.\nAfter the coup succeeded, he declared an evacuation from Planet S-1, loading the citizenry aboard the giant battleship Algol and carrying out a warp to a new world. Upon finding Earth, the first habitable planet discovered, he decided to make it their new homeworld and ordered an attack to exterminate humanity.\nThough generous toward his own people, he has a ruthless side as well, unhesitatingly discarding subordinates who fail him if it serves his goals. But even this stems from the mission he set for himself - saving the people of Planet S-1 - and his iron will never wavered to the end.\nHe dotes on Aphrodia, both his subordinate and something of a surrogate daughter, and places immense trust in her. He has entrusted her with full authority over the invasion of Earth, while he himself waits in the subspace fortress for word of the operation's success.",
        81: "A staff officer in the Aldebaron military.\nThough outwardly deferential to Gattler, he is an ambitious man scheming to topple him from the Fuhrer's seat and rise to the top of Planet S-1's people should the opportunity arise.\nHe harbors a deep-seated hatred for Aphrodia, who let his twin brother Garo die in the Himalayas. Using the relationship between Earth and Planet S-1, a secret Gattler keeps tightly hidden, as leverage, he pulled Aphrodia down from her post as commander-in-chief and installed himself in her place.",
        82: "An Aldebaron officer who secretly fed information about his own side to Blue Fixer.\nHe has been Marin's close friend since childhood, having studied together with him at UF Museion, a university on Planet S-1. However, a rift formed in their friendship over a matter involving the awarding of a degree, and Flick disappeared from Marin's life afterward.\nHe currently serves in the Aldebaron military, waiting for a chance to avenge comrades executed during Aldebaron's coup. After obtaining the location of an important secret factory, he sought asylum on Earth and made contact with Marin using the battle mecha Silver Shark. By the time the two reunited, the old rift between them was gone, and they swore together to defeat Gattler.",
        83: "Emperor of Planet S-1.\nA gentle man by nature, he supported the group of scientists working to restore the radiation-contaminated environment.\nHowever, under pressure from the military at the Supreme Council, Gattler forced him to agree that if the radiation filtration and circulation system was not completed within a set deadline, the military would be dispatched to another planet.\nBut this was not enough to satisfy Gattler, who secretly plotted a coup. On the very night the system was completed, the emperor was assassinated in his bedroom by Aphrodia, acting under secret orders.",
        84: "The second son of the Jin family and main pilot of Zambot 3. Twelve years old, a first-year middle school student.\nA local delinquent notorious for constant fighting and riding a motorcycle without a license, but at heart he is kind and cannot bear to leave anyone in trouble.\nUsing piloting knowledge learned through sleep-learning, along with his natural athleticism and sharp instincts, he handles the Zambird, Zambo Ace, and Zambot 3 as extensions of his own body. Even so, he grew increasingly frustrated that the people around him failed to understand him despite his desperate fight against the Gaizock. But through witnessing the Gaizock's escalating campaign of destruction and merciless tactics like human bombs, and through reconciling with those he had clashed with, he grew as a person.",
        85: "The eldest son of the Kamie family and pilot of the Zambull. Fifteen years old, a third-year middle school student.\nHe has a cynical air and look about him, but like Kappei, he is warmhearted underneath. Intelligent and quick-witted, he sometimes devised strategies that contributed to victory. He has a younger brother named Kazuyuki and a younger sister named Kiiro, both of whom look up to him as a good older brother.\nUnlike the other Jin Family households, his has what might be called an overbearing 'education mom' for a mother, one who tries to protect only her own life and possessions with no regard for those around her, and Uchuta felt a sense of guilt over this. He once clashed with Kappei after Kappei mocked him for it, but the two deepened their bond through the fighting that followed.",
        86: "The eldest daughter of the Kamikita family and pilot of the Zambase. A second-year middle school student, thirteen years old through episode eleven.\nHer family runs a ranch in Shinshu, and she is a beautiful, lively, and easygoing girl whose talents are horseback riding and archery. She has a younger sister named Kimiko, who is introverted and bears no resemblance to her, in either looks or personality.\nWhen she returned to her hometown for her birthday, she, like the other members of the Jin Family, was resented by her old friends for reasons that were not her fault, and was shown to have a vulnerable side, taking the rejection hard. But drawing strength from her mother's feelings, she recovered, and her friends came to see the truth and reconcile with her after witnessing her continue rescue efforts even while wounded by stray gunfire. This inner strength is truly her defining trait.",
        87: "Keiko's grandfather. Seventy-five years old.\nAs something of an elder statesman of the Jin Family, he holds the group together with strong will and conviction as they face the Gaizock.\nHe and Umee, a trusted advisor to the family, are cousins, but the fact that he once gave her a rice bowl as a gift in his younger days suggests there may have been something more between them.\nHe also provides the narration for the next-episode previews, memorably closing each one with the line, \"Now then, how will they fight their way through this time?\"",
        88: "Kappei's father. Forty-eight years old.\nA fishing boat owner who runs Jin Fisheries in Suruga Bay. After Beal I was discovered, he took command of it as its captain during battle.\nThough strict by nature, he holds deep love for his wife and children, a man of the sea overflowing with warmth and manly spirit. Having often been away from home for deep-sea fishing, he knows well the value of time spent together with family.",
        89: "Kappei's older brother. Seventeen years old.\nSerious and mild-mannered in contrast to his brother, he is in charge of combat command aboard Beal I and King Beal.\nPossessed of sharp insight, he discovered Zambot 3's combination system. At one point, to discipline Kappei and the others for their lack of coordination, he brought the Zambo Ace to a halt and forced them to agree to combine by threatening, \"If the Jin Family can't fight without unity, then we might as well all die together\" - a bold and quick-witted move on his part.",
        90: "Kappei's grandmother. Sixty-eight years old.\nShe serves as an advisor to the Jin Family, and even Heizaemon places complete trust in her.\nA spry old woman who never seems her age, she loves rock music and once even suited up in battle gear to sortie herself in order to save Nozaki, her first love.",
        91: "Kappei's mother. Thirty-five years old.\nBold and big-hearted, just as she appears.\nHer love for her two sons and her husband is plain to see, and when Kazuki fired a gun at her out of misplaced resentment, she showed both strength and motherly resolve by slapping him without fear of the weapon, setting him straight.",
        92: "Kappei's beloved dog, named Nishiki for the flower-petal pattern on his forehead.\nHe rides along with Kappei in the Zambird's right-hand cockpit during sorties. In time he came to take over Kappei's 'Woof!' call during combination sequences.",
        93: "The leader of the delinquent Kazuki Gang, a boy who was at odds with Kappei.\nIn a Gaizock attack, he was separated from his parents and his younger sister Kaoru. Believing the Jin Family was to blame, he harbored intense hatred toward them.\nBut after witnessing the Gaizock's merciless tactics, such as human bombs, he gradually changed his outlook. He was later caught in a crisis that nearly turned him into a human bomb himself, but escaped thanks in part to Kappei's efforts. When the two were reunited, they shared a heartfelt handshake, and from then on Kazuki cooperated with Kappei, ultimately joining the Jin Family in the journey to space for the final battle.",
    },
}
